\id 3JN Verification fixture for verify-pipeline
\ide UTF-8
\h 3 JOHN
\toc1 3 John
\toc2 3 John
\toc3 3jn
\mt1 3 JOHN

\c 1
\p
\v 1 The elder writes to the the beloved friend, whom he loves in truth.
\v 2 Truly, truly, he prays that all goes well with him.
\v 3 He was glad when brothers came and spoke of his faithfulness.
\v 4 No joy is greater than to hear that his children walk in truth.
\v 5 Beloved, you act faithfully in what you do for the brothers and strangers.
\v 6 They spoke of your love before the church.
\v 7 For they went out for the sake of the Name, taking nothing from the Gentiles.
\v 8 So we ought to support such men, that we may be fellow workers for the truth.
\v 9 I wrote something to the churсh, but Diotrephes does not receive us.
\v 10 So if I come, I will bring up what he does, talking against us with wicked words.
\v 11 Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but what is good.
\v 12 Démetrius has received a good report from everyone, and from the truth itself.
\v 13 I had many things to write to you, but I do not wish to write with pen and ink.
\v 14 I hope to see you soon, and we will speak face to face.
\v 15 Peace be to you. The friends greet you. Greet the friends by name.
